  "title": "The SBA Just Rolled Over on Rollover Equity",
  "date": "2025-04-28T14:31:24.458Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n The SBA Just Rolled Over on Rollover Equity\nSara,\nHeads up, buyers and sellers\u2014especially the ones eyeing a little equity rollover in your next deal.\nThe SBA\u2019s latest revision to SOP 50 10 8 (effective June 1, 2025) just dropped, and it comes with a curveball that could change the way deals are structured.\nHere\u2019s the big news:\nIf a seller keeps any equity\u2014yes, even 1%\u2014they now have to personally guarantee the entire SBA 7(a) loan. Not just their sliver of the pie. The whole thing. And that personal guarantee sticks around for two years after the deal closes.\nPreviously, this only kicked in if you owned 20% or more. So yes, this is a big shift. One that could make some sellers think twice before hanging onto a small piece of the business.\nWhat does this mean for deals?\nWell, we\u2019re likely going to see:\nMore caution with rollover equity. If you thought you\u2019d keep a toe in the water without getting soaked\u2014surprise! You're swimming in the deep end now.\n\nA stronger push for outside capital. Think investor-backed deals, seller notes structured outside SBA guidelines, or other creative financing workarounds.\n\nThis also means SBA lenders are going to be extra nosy about your deal structure. So if you're the buyer, make sure your legal and lending teams are in sync. And if you\u2019re the seller\u2014know what you\u2019re signing up for.\nOf course, we\u2019ve seen SOPs evolve before. It\u2019s entirely possible this gets softened or reinterpreted later. But for now, this is theoretically going to be the rule. \nNeed help navigating SBA rules or deal structuring? That\u2019s kind of our thing.\nUntil next time\u2014make smart deals and skip the surprises,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant & Founder of Deal Academy\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers podcast episodes by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
